## 5751ed9bdf85

**Conclusion: Reproduced defect — fail-open public scalar surface.** Audited generator SHA-256: `b11102ec70073d50cd748858e6f631d4be643c8c280a33feb6ef379ea2c61b38`. No source was modified.

The combined audit snapshot completed both requested stages. Its portable task tests passed 10/10. The semantic gate returned `WARN`, not a clean pass, because one searched generic rival remained compatible with one sampled easy-band lesson; nevertheless all 12 declared lessons materialized, all 60 query rotations were unambiguous, all five canonical pairs were usable, both declared canonical shortcuts fit those canonical pairs, and generated witnesses refuted them. See `checks/audit/5751ed9bdf85-combined/checks/5751ed9bdf85_audit_summary.json` and `..._audit_semantic_gate.json`.

A separate strict defect-lint run found 111 accepted invalid scalar values, repeated over easy/default/hard probes:

- `seed`: 15 accepted invalid values;
- `sample_index`: 18, including booleans, floats, strings, and `-1`;
- `grid_h`: 18 numeric strings/floats;
- `grid_w`: 18 numeric strings/floats;
- `decoy_marker_count`: 18 numeric strings/floats;
- `target_color`: 24 booleans, strings, and floats.

This is actionable because declared exact controls and call coordinates should reject malformed scalar types rather than normalize them silently. Full source-bound evidence is `checks/audit/5751ed9bdf85-defect-lint/result.json`; the concise findings are in `checks/audit/5751ed9bdf85-defect-lint/checks/5751ed9bdf85_audit_defect_lint.log`. Audit does not approve a repair.
